		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2035&amp;p=33420#p33420"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>I have been battling installation for 3 days. I could not get my USB A to mini USB cable to be recognized by Windows 11. I tried everything, I thought. However, I finally got it to work by turning off core isolation/memory integrity in Windows 11. It works normally with this off. But, I really don't want to leave this off. Does anyone know of an updated driver for USB mini cables for Windows 11, or any other setting that would make the cable compatible with Windows 11 with the security settings enabled?<br><br>I still have not installed OpenGD77, but at least I can communicate with the radio now.</div></blockquote>Which driver are you using.<br><br>Did you try the one on this site<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/drivers/" class="postlink">downloads/drivers/</a><br><br><br><br>If you did use that driver...<br><br>I did a quick search and found this thread on Microsoft's  Answers forum<br><br><a href="https://answers.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/forum/all/sttub30sys-stmicroelectronics-incompatible-driver/9acf3a29-6069-4418-8ddf-72f9551ded8d" class="postlink">https://answers.microsoft.com/en-us/win ... f9551ded8d</a><br><br>Which suggests that one of the files has a newer version</div></blockquote>That driver worked. However, it took some time to figure out how to delete the drivers that I had already tried and installed that were incompatible. The add or remove device tool would not remove the sttub30.sys. I ended up going to cmd prompt as administrator and force removed it once I knew what the files real name was in the system with a .inf ending. But, thank you. The new driver works with all of the Windows 11 core security enabled.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7030">K4URO</a> — Thu Oct 10, 2024 1:08 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
